Can you change this to the following?

```suggestion
  public clear() {
    commonClear();
    this.state.reset();
  }
```

Some older versions of Safari can have difficulties with parenthesis in field initializes, see https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Classes/Public_class_fields

And it's generally better to use a class method vs an arrow function associated with an instance.

**suggestion(non-blocking)**: Is it worth having something like this instead?

The `throw new Error('');` should never happen.

```suggestion
      const db = parser.parser?.yy;
      if (!(db instanceof TreemapDB)) {
        throw new Error('parser.parser?.yy was not a TreemapDB. This is due to a bug within Mermaid, please report this issue at https://github.com/mermaid-js/mermaid/issues.');
      }
      populate(ast, db);
```

**non-blocking** since the current code should be safe too, I just really don't like using `as XXXXXX` if I can avoid it.
